---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="China Transport Guide: Trains, Metro & Didi"
  description="Navigate China like a pro: high-speed trains between clothing cities, costs, trip.com booking tips, metro systems, and Didi ride-hailing for travelers."
  canonicalUrl="/plan-trip/transport"
  articleDate="2026-08-03"
  breadcrumbs={{ name: "Home", url: "/" }, { name: "Plan Your Trip", url: "/plan-trip/" }, { name: "Transport Guide", url: "/plan-trip/transport/" }}>
  <section class="pt-24 pb-16"><div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <span class="text-xs font-medium text-[#b5343a] tracking-[0.15em] uppercase">Plan Your Trip · Transport</span>
    <h1 class="font-serif-sc text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight text-stone-900 mt-3">Getting Around China: Trains, Metros & Apps</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-stone-500 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">China''s high-speed rail network covers every city in our guide. It''s fast, punctual, and half the price of equivalent European or Japanese trains.</p>
    <h2 class="font-serif-sc text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-16 mb-4">Key Train Routes for Your Trip</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto"><table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse"><thead><tr class="border-b border-stone-200 text-left"><th class="py-3 pr-4 font-semibold">Route</th><th class="py-3 pr-4 font-semibold">Duration</th><th class="py-3 pr-4 font-semibold">2nd Class</th><th class="py-3 pr-4 font-semibold">1st Class</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Beijing to Xi''an</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">4.5 hrs</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">515 RMB</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">825 RMB</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Xi''an to Chengdu</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">3 hrs</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">263 RMB</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">420 RMB</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Shanghai to Suzhou</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">25 min</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">40 RMB</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">70 RMB</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Shanghai to Hangzhou</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">45 min</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">73 RMB</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">117 RMB</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Hangzhou to Nanjing</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">1.5 hrs</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">118 RMB</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">189 RMB</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Beijing to Shanghai</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">4.5 hrs</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">553 RMB</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">930 RMB</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
    <h2 class="font-serif-sc text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-14 mb-4">How to Book</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-4"><strong>trip.com</strong> — English interface, foreign cards accepted, small booking fee (10-30 RMB). Best for first-time visitors. Book 1-2 weeks ahead. <strong>12306</strong> — official app, no booking fee but Chinese-only. You need a Chinese phone number.</p>
    <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-4"><strong>At the station:</strong> Arrive 45 min before, security check, passport needed. Gate opens 15 min before, closes 5 min before. Trains leave exactly on time.</p>
    <h2 class="font-serif-sc text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-14 mb-4">Within Cities</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-4"><strong>Metro:</strong> Every city has a modern system, English signage, 3-9 RMB/ride. <strong>Didi:</strong> China''s Uber, English app, pay through the app, 15-40 RMB for cross-city trips.</p>
    <div class="mt-8"><a href="/plan-trip" class="text-sm text-stone-400 hover:text-stone-600 transition-colors">Back to Plan Your Trip</a></div>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
